### Drafting a proposal.
###
### Run auth.http first, log in as tourpro, and paste the token below.
### Requires ANTHROPIC_API_KEY in the server's environment. Without it every call
### here returns 400 "Drafting is not configured on this server.", which is the
### designed behaviour and not a failure.
###
### The five PENDING requests in the seed data, with the confirmed trips behind
### each destination. More history means more for the model to price from.
###
###   53  dest  7   4 past trips   8 players, 3 rounds, 2 nights, $400/player
###   52  dest 10   2 past trips   6 players, 3 rounds, 2 nights, $550/player
###   56  dest 14   2 past trips  12 players, 2 rounds, 2 nights, $500/player
###   54  dest 15   1 past trip    4 players, 2 rounds, 2 nights, $425/player
###   55  dest  5   1 past trip    4 players, 3 rounds, 1 night,  $350/player

@host = http://localhost:8080
@token = paste-tourpro-token-here
@clientToken = paste-a-client-token-here

### The queue, to confirm what is actually pending.
GET {{host}}/api/host/request
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Best first test: the most history to draw on.
POST {{host}}/api/host/request/53/proposal/draft
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Thinnest history. Worth comparing: one past trip is much less to price from,
### and the rationale should be more hedged if the prompt is doing its job.
POST {{host}}/api/host/request/55/proposal/draft
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Twelve players, which no past trip at that destination matches. Tests whether
### it scales the price or just copies a number.
POST {{host}}/api/host/request/56/proposal/draft
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### A request already PROPOSED rather than PENDING: 400, no model call, no spend.
POST {{host}}/api/host/request/51/proposal/draft
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### As a client: 403 from SecurityConfig, before it reaches any of this.
POST {{host}}/api/host/request/53/proposal/draft
Authorization: Bearer {{clientToken}}

### The decline-with-no-history path is NOT reachable from seed data -- every
### pending request has a destination with confirmed trips. To see it, create a
### request naming a place nobody has booked, then draft against its id.
POST {{host}}/api/request
Authorization: Bearer {{clientToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "requestedPlace": "Bandon Dunes",
  "budgetPerPlayer": 900.00,
  "playerCount": 4,
  "roundsRequested": 2,
  "nights": 3,
  "earliestStart": "2027-05-03",
  "latestStart": "2027-05-10"
}
